{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>ויחזק.</b> Smooths, from the root of ואנכי איש חלק (Genesis 27:11)." "<b>פטיש.</b> Known, like וכפטיש יפוץ סלע (Jeremiah 23:29)." "<b>הולם פעם.</b> From the root of והלמה מסיסרא (Judges 5:26), and it is the iron upon which one strikes with it, and פעם may possibly be the iron tool upon which they strike, and it is called פעם because one strikes upon it (פעם), or 'הולם פעם' is one tool." "<b>אומר לדבק.</b> Until the glue is good."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra reads ויחזק as 'smooths/polishes,' deriving it from the root ח-ל-ק."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:20.104368887Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}